<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16406" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurytus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔρυτος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>King of Oechalia and father of Iole</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9,
				356</span></i>.—Whence <i>Iole</i> is called
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurytis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9,
				395</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 9, 133</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A centaur</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				220</span></i>.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurytĭon</span></b> ,
			ōnis, m., <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1,
				593</span></i> (cf. Hom. Od. 21, 285).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An Argonaut</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl.
				1, 439 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
